AM Configurator incorporates protocol implementation work adapted from
cyberboard-cli by GeneralD (https://github.com/GeneralD/cyberboard-cli), used
under the MIT License. The adapted work informs the CyberBoard keymap and LED
frame protocol handling, principally in am_configurator/device_mapping.py,
am_configurator/device.py, and am_configurator/writer.py. GeneralD's original
copyright notice and the full MIT license text are preserved in
licenses/cyberboard-cli-LICENSE.txt.

The AM Neon 80 axial LED payload ordering in am_configurator/device_mapping.py
is derived from src/804/axialDefinitionsData.ts in AngryMiao/neon80_driver,
Copyright (c) Angry Miao, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). What is used is the interface
fact that file records — which payload index lights which physical LED — with
its CSS pixel coordinates reduced to grid positions. No source code from that
project is copied or distributed here.

Native AM Configurator distributions include a constrained, network-disabled build
of FFmpeg 8.1.2, Copyright (c) the FFmpeg developers, under the GNU Lesser
General Public License version 2.1 or later. The license text, pinned official
source, detached-signature information, reproducible build recipe, and source
offer are included under packaging/ffmpeg/.
